1
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:07,880
Hey, Ama.

2
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,980
What is it?

3
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:20,110
I think we should... break up.

4
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,170
What do you mean?

5
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:30,700
I've had enough fun.

6
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:33,850
What?

7
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:39,660
That's the kind of guy I am.

8
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:43,460
You know that, right?

9
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:50,670
I want my spare key back.

10
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,360
Don't come back.

11
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:58,094
- Wait, Chiaki!
- I'm thinking of getting back to work soon.

12
00:00:59,230 --> 00:01:01,650
I don't want you holding me back.

13
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:17,950
Goodbye, Ama.

14
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:37,160
You wouldn't understand how I feel.

15
00:02:37,790 --> 00:02:39,400
Yeah, I don't.

16
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:42,080
And I don't want to understand.

17
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:44,940
I didn't know either.

18
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:47,720
Not until I met him...

19
00:02:50,510 --> 00:02:53,480
- Cut.
- Cut.

20
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,964
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

21
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:06,400
How are things with Chiaki?

22
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:11,200
Sorry.

23
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:14,490
I'm not the type to make small talk.

24
00:03:18,150 --> 00:03:20,540
We broke up.

25
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,830
What?

26
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:41,600
I'll come by again, okay?

27
00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:52,860
Why didn't you answer my texts?

28
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:55,650
Sorry.

29
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:58,680
I'm going for drinks with Seira now.

30
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:00,711
Come clear your head.

31
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:09,130
Come on. Let's go.

32
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,130
Hey there.

33
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:21,350
So you're here too.

34
00:04:22,770 --> 00:04:25,410
I invited him.

35
00:04:25,410 --> 00:04:29,690
Since I'm back in Japan,
I wanna drink with everyone.

36
00:04:29,690 --> 00:04:34,850
We were classmates,
so let's keep being friends, okay?

37
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,850
Oh, right.

38
00:04:42,850 --> 00:04:45,860
Why did you break up with Ama, Chiaki?

39
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:47,170
Huh?

40
00:04:47,170 --> 00:04:48,490
What?

41
00:04:48,490 --> 00:04:51,380
She looked down.

42
00:04:52,590 --> 00:04:54,460
What happened?

43
00:04:56,320 --> 00:05:00,850
Could it be because of your mother?

44
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:11,210
I realized...

45
00:05:12,460 --> 00:05:15,780
we're just too different.

46
00:05:18,650 --> 00:05:20,880
If Ama dates me,

47
00:05:22,430 --> 00:05:24,830
she'll only end up unhappy.

48
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:32,200
That doesn't mean you have to break up.

49
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,300
That makes no sense.

50
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:41,800
You don't have to understand.

51
00:05:48,610 --> 00:05:53,860
You should tell Ama how you really feel.

52
00:05:55,450 --> 00:06:00,100
I'm sure she'll accept you.

53
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,740
I don't want to give her trouble.

54
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,500
So...

55
00:06:13,170 --> 00:06:16,130
I don't have to give up on Ama, then?

56
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:24,220
If you two broke up, it's fine then, right?

57
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,640
I'm going home.

58
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,450
- Hey, wait.
- Chiaki.

59
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:51,830
With that last scene,
Ms. Seira and Ms. Minase, that's a wrap!

60
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:57,210
Thank you very much.

61
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:01,180
- Ms. Seira.
- Good work, everyone.

62
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:03,430
Thank you very much.

63
00:07:08,250 --> 00:07:12,870
I think you're the only one who can save him.

64
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:20,280
Good work.

65
00:07:35,370 --> 00:07:36,910
See you.

66
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:45,120
Whew, glad it's over.

67
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,830
Yes.

68
00:07:46,830 --> 00:07:49,700
The director praised your acting.

69
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:52,730
I'll keep doing my best!

70
00:07:52,730 --> 00:07:54,020
I'll go get the car.

71
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:56,000
Thank you.

72
00:07:58,390 --> 00:07:59,820
Ama.

73
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,350
Kairi-senpai.

74
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:04,790
Long time no see.

75
00:08:04,790 --> 00:08:06,965
Long time no see.

76
00:08:06,965 --> 00:08:09,740
Kairi-senpai, why are you here?

77
00:08:10,583 --> 00:08:13,540
I was filming nearby.

78
00:08:14,310 --> 00:08:15,840
No...

79
00:08:16,970 --> 00:08:18,590
That's a lie.

80
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,650
I came to tell you something.

81
00:08:25,310 --> 00:08:27,450
Tell me something?

82
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:30,850
I...

83
00:08:33,066 --> 00:08:35,466
I still love you, Ama.

84
00:08:37,601 --> 00:08:40,161
I'd do anything for you.

85
00:08:40,830 --> 00:08:42,560
No one else...

86
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:46,060
can make you happier but me.

87
00:08:48,290 --> 00:08:49,940
That's...

88
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,190
what I used to think.

89
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:59,280
If that scumbag had stayed a scumbag,

90
00:09:00,710 --> 00:09:04,330
I might have had a chance.

91
00:09:04,330 --> 00:09:07,850
Well, I don't know what happened,

92
00:09:07,850 --> 00:09:12,490
but I think he still loves you.

93
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:15,340
Huh?

94
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:16,810
See you.

95
00:09:55,860 --> 00:10:00,180
<i>Make sure you have the money ready.</i>

96
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:14,870
<i>I still want to talk things through.</i>

97
00:10:14,870 --> 00:10:17,290
<i>I want to see you one more time.</i>

98
00:10:32,710 --> 00:10:34,230
Come in.

99
00:10:50,730 --> 00:10:53,880
I wanted to know...

100
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:55,800
what I did wrong.

101
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:01,100
You didn't do anything wrong, Ama.

102
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:06,290
Then why did you want to break up?

103
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:12,800
Because you and I are different.

104
00:11:15,890 --> 00:11:19,030
I'll do my best...

105
00:11:19,030 --> 00:11:21,930
- to be good enough for you.
- No.

106
00:11:23,090 --> 00:11:24,900
You don't get it.

107
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:29,860
Then what is it?

108
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:37,520
I'm nothing but trouble.

109
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:40,210
That's why...

110
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,850
I'll only cause you trouble.

111
00:11:46,910 --> 00:11:49,320
Nothing but trouble?

112
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:53,050
Who told you that?

113
00:11:56,300 --> 00:11:59,220
I was trouble the moment I was born.

114
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:01,710
No.

115
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:03,850
That's not true.

116
00:12:03,850 --> 00:12:06,380
- Chiaki.
- It's true!

117
00:12:07,110 --> 00:12:08,830
The moment that woman birthed me...

118
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:11,690
There's no way that's true, Chiaki.

119
00:12:12,870 --> 00:12:15,110
I was a struggling idol,

120
00:12:15,110 --> 00:12:19,060
but I had to work hard for my family.

121
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,580
Sometimes,

122
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:26,370
it felt like running through
a tunnel with no end in sight.

123
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:30,740
But...

124
00:12:34,490 --> 00:12:37,720
you saved me.

125
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:41,220
Hey,

126
00:12:42,090 --> 00:12:43,970
Chiaki.

127
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:53,220
Now...

128
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:55,830
- it's my turn to...
- Go home.

129
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:01,580
Chiaki.

130
00:13:03,540 --> 00:13:06,840
Chiaki! Hey, Chiaki!

131
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:10,410
You're not a helpless kid anymore!

132
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:13,010
And...

133
00:13:14,090 --> 00:13:16,550
you're not alone anymore!

134
00:13:16,550 --> 00:13:20,570
I'll always be by your side.

135
00:13:20,570 --> 00:13:23,170
Just remember that.

136
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:27,270
Please.

137
00:13:49,310 --> 00:13:51,000
Here.

138
00:13:52,270 --> 00:13:54,850
See, I knew you had the money.

139
00:14:21,630 --> 00:14:25,600
Hey, isn't this a little short?

140
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:31,010
You've been spending your money
on that woman, huh?

141
00:14:31,010 --> 00:14:32,510
That woman?

142
00:14:32,510 --> 00:14:34,860
Ama Minase.

143
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:37,400
So that's why she was so persistent.

144
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:39,300
Huh?

145
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:41,740
I saw her here the other day.

146
00:15:04,510 --> 00:15:05,830
What?

147
00:15:05,830 --> 00:15:07,930
You're going to Chiaki's place, right?

148
00:15:07,930 --> 00:15:12,590
- Let go.
- Please, stop tormenting Chiaki!

149
00:15:12,590 --> 00:15:14,390
What are you talking about?

150
00:15:14,390 --> 00:15:20,430
Please! Please!

151
00:15:20,430 --> 00:15:22,310
You're so annoying.

152
00:15:22,310 --> 00:15:25,091
Chiaki's been struggling for so long.

153
00:15:25,091 --> 00:15:26,230
So, please...

154
00:15:26,230 --> 00:15:28,380
Stop it!

155
00:15:30,270 --> 00:15:33,190
Your popularity's going up, huh?

156
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:39,570
A slut who's always hanging around
with a certain scumbag.

157
00:15:39,570 --> 00:15:42,990
Maybe I'll tip off a weekly magazine.

158
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:47,140
You're an idol too, aren't you?

159
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:49,970
- That would be bad for you...
- Go ahead.

160
00:15:49,970 --> 00:15:50,990
Huh?

161
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:54,110
If that will save Chiaki,

162
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:57,250
I don't care what happens to me.

163
00:15:59,670 --> 00:16:01,230
Oh, really.

164
00:16:01,230 --> 00:16:03,920
Then let it happen.

165
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:06,790
Hey, let go!

166
00:16:06,790 --> 00:16:09,140
If you keep this up,

167
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:12,640
I don't know what I'll do to you.

168
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:14,270
Huh?

169
00:16:15,928 --> 00:16:19,838
I'm serious.

170
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:31,290
Ow, let go!

171
00:16:31,290 --> 00:16:33,600
It hurts!

172
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:35,360
Hey!

173
00:16:37,350 --> 00:16:40,820
That woman is insane.

174
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:45,220
Ama...

175
00:16:51,090 --> 00:16:53,070
Listen up.

176
00:16:55,730 --> 00:17:00,420
Don't get any strange ideas about leaving me.

177
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:03,570
If you understand, answer me.

178
00:17:07,430 --> 00:17:10,280
Answer me!

179
00:17:16,690 --> 00:17:21,210
Stop it already.

180
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:23,500
Hey.

181
00:17:27,030 --> 00:17:31,110
You'd hit your own mother?

182
00:17:31,110 --> 00:17:33,000
No.

183
00:17:33,950 --> 00:17:38,630
I want to, but I can't.

184
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,930
You knew that, didn't you?

185
00:17:43,110 --> 00:17:47,350
<i>No matter how much I hate you,
you're still my mother.</i>

186
00:17:50,690 --> 00:17:52,890
Let go.

187
00:17:52,890 --> 00:17:54,310
Let go of me!

188
00:17:54,310 --> 00:17:57,240
Your life turning into a mess...

189
00:17:57,930 --> 00:18:00,000
That wasn't my fault.

190
00:18:01,020 --> 00:18:03,240
I finally realized.

191
00:18:04,111 --> 00:18:08,481
I'm not a helpless kid anymore.

192
00:18:11,450 --> 00:18:13,270
What?

193
00:18:13,270 --> 00:18:18,190
You and that woman
both treat me like the villain...

194
00:18:18,190 --> 00:18:20,250
Promise me.

195
00:18:20,250 --> 00:18:22,650
Promise you'll stay out of my life.

196
00:18:29,210 --> 00:18:31,070
Stay away.

197
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,070
If you don't,

198
00:18:38,970 --> 00:18:41,870
I don't know what I'll do to you.

199
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:51,660
Okay...

200
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,010
Okay, fine!

201
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:31,450
Ama.

202
00:19:39,310 --> 00:19:41,540
I heard from my mother.

203
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:47,920
Why would you go that far for me?

204
00:19:50,070 --> 00:19:53,300
Because you saved me.

205
00:19:55,050 --> 00:19:58,270
Now I want to save you.

206
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:01,700
That's all.

207
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:08,640
I'm sorry.

208
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:12,930
I'm sorry, Ama.

209
00:20:19,830 --> 00:20:23,170
I'm a hopeless scumbag.

210
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:30,030
And I was afraid
that someday you'd leave me.

211
00:20:30,030 --> 00:20:31,970
That's what I thought.

212
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:47,500
I won't leave.

213
00:20:51,510 --> 00:20:53,660
No matter what you're like,

214
00:20:54,730 --> 00:20:57,630
I'll accept all of you.

215
00:21:06,070 --> 00:21:07,940
Ama...

216
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:16,510
Thank you for saving me.

217
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:46,620
And now, the star of "Einen",
Mr. Chiaki Hosho.

218
00:21:46,620 --> 00:21:48,420
I'm Chiaki Hosho.

219
00:21:48,420 --> 00:21:51,035
I'll give it my all.

220
00:21:51,035 --> 00:21:54,215
Now entering the lead actress,
Ms. Ama Minase!

221
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:56,980
I'm Ama Minase.

222
00:21:56,980 --> 00:21:58,630
Thank you for having me.

223
00:21:58,630 --> 00:22:00,950
Nice to meet you.

224
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:06,116
Everyone, dinner's ready!

225
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:07,660
Let's go.

226
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:11,248
- Meat and potato stew! Yay!
- There's plenty!

227
00:22:24,810 --> 00:22:26,800
Hey, Chiaki.

228
00:22:29,970 --> 00:22:31,650
Yes?

229
00:22:36,230 --> 00:22:40,060
I'll do anything for you, Chiaki.

230
00:22:41,650 --> 00:22:46,210
So, stay by my side forever.

